      "fileName": "poultice-preparation.json",
      "id": "4BbfHsGPRHPHfIGY",
      "name": "Poultice Preparation",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "4BbfHsGPRHPHfIGY",
        "folder": "RM5KwlKBN3uKTcd8",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Poultice Preparation",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>When you create an herbal elixir, you can prepare it as a poultice instead. A poultice gains the oil trait (but remains alchemical, not magical) and loses the elixir and ingested traits. You can apply a poultice by @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Interact]{Interacting} with one hand.</p>\n<p>When you apply a poultice, in addition to the item's normal effects, the recipient can attempt an immediate flat check to recover from a single source of persistent acid, bleed, or fire damage, with the DC reduction from appropriate assistance.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Herbalist Dedication"
              }
            ]
          },
